 ## Safety rules for women and night-shift employees
 
 ### Essential safety SOPs
 
 Employers have a duty-of-care heightened during heavy rain and night operations. Implement these mandatory rules:
 
-- **Verified drivers:** Only drivers with background checks and up-to-date ID assigned to night or monsoon runs.  
-- **Two-person check-in:** Driver and operations manager confirm pickup list before departure.  
-- **Safe-drop policy:** Do not leave female employees at unsheltered locations; drop only at verified, lit points.  
-- **Buddy/paired pickups:** Where possible, group late-night pickups so employees arrive in pairs or small groups.  
-- **Real-time tracking share:** Share live vehicle location and ETA with passengers and their reporting manager.  
-- **Emergency kit:** Every vehicle carries torches, first-aid, and an umbrella stash; drivers trained in basic rescue exits.  
-- **Escalation protocol:** Immediate contact with operations if water levels rise; pre-authorised diversion to safe shelter points.
+- Verified drivers: Only drivers with background checks and up-to-date ID assigned to night or monsoon runs.  
+- Two-person check-in: Driver and operations manager confirm pickup list before departure.  
+- Safe-drop policy: Do not leave female employees at unsheltered locations; drop only at verified, lit points.  
+- Buddy/paired pickups: Where possible, group late-night pickups so employees arrive in pairs or small groups.  
+- Real-time tracking share: Share live vehicle location and ETA with passengers and their reporting manager.  
+- Emergency kit: Every vehicle carries torches, first-aid, and an umbrella stash; drivers trained in basic rescue exits.  
